AliasMode: behind a proxy without UDP (an HTTP proxy), show the ICE agent
stock Firefox on the identity's network shows instead of a machine whose UDP is
blocked: host candidates, a srflx with the identity's address after the round
trip through the proxy from a STUN server that could answer, the errors and
timings nICEr gives the others, and checks that fail. None of it sends a
packet. Behind a SOCKS5 proxy with UDP the real agent works through the
proxy's UDP relay (webrtc-socks5-udp.patch) and this never starts. The choice
follows the context's proxy only, so every connection of a context shows the
same network: with a TURN server over TCP or TLS, which the real agent reaches
through the proxy, the real agent gathers and checks, and this adds what the
UDP servers give (the srflx and the errors). aliasmode:webrtcFakeIce false
turns it off.

